{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VPviTUSj8n6SEQicP2ptRA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Native decomposition and review\n2\t\n3\tUse `taskspec decompose prepare <id> --recipe <file>` to validate authored input\n4\tand propose topology. `--dry-run` produces diagnostics without changing the plan.\n5\tEach accepted seam owns one swimlane; each capability leg names an observable\n6\tstate and proof; executable leaves own coherent done-conditions and bounded writes.\n7\tSDLC stages are concerns on the work, not mandatory lanes.\n8\t\n9\tA blocked proposal is a valid planning outcome. Preserve `OPEN` objections and\n10\t`system_map.unknowns` when ownership, evidence, or product decisions are missing.\n11\tKeep the authored proposal and report the smallest unresolved decision; do not\n12\tclear unknowns or mark objections `ACCEPTED` or `FIXED` merely to make preparation\n13\tpass. Record resolution or accepted risk only from an explicit applicable decision.\n14\tThe reviewer's identity authenticates review; it does not assign seam or swimlane\n15\townership. Record actual owners in the recipe and prepare the corrected topology\n16\tbefore requesting review.\n17\t\n18\tRead `tasks/.plans/<id>/delivery-plan.yaml`, proposed leg artifacts, and graph\n19\tbefore recording explicit human review:\n20\t\n21\t```bash\n22\ttaskspec decompose review <id> --accept --reviewer <identity> --reason <decision>\n23\ttaskspec decompose compile <id>\n24\ttaskspec plan --manifest tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n25\ttaskspec batch --plan tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n26\t```\n27\t\n28\tReview binds the complete topology through the repository HMAC key using the\n29\tplan-review domain. Compilation and materialization do not seal execution.\n30\tThe authored recipe, immutable snapshots, native TaskPlanLineage/v1, bundle,\n31\tand existing materialization receipt retain the intent-to-leaf chain.\n32\t\n33\tBefore replanning, preserve the prior bundle path. Use `prepare --replace`, review,\n34\tcompile, then `decompose impact <id> --against <prior-bundle.json>` to inspect\n35\tchanged, added, removed, and unchanged projections. Relevant constraints, recipe,\n36\tdependencies, proof, and source changes require renewed authorization. Unrelated\n37\tsibling changes preserve the earlier snapshot for unchanged leaves.\n38\t\n39\tRecipe task fields may include `execution_recipe` (a strategy name),\n40\t`shared_resources` (resource identifiers requiring serialization), and\n41\t`proves_capabilities` (leg IDs this integration-proof leaf independently evaluates).\n42\tAbsence of a proof leaf leaves a capability unproven even when all children are done.\n43\t\n44\tOptional `sdlc_stages` values are `plan`, `design`, `build`, `test`, `deploy`, and\n45\t`maintain`. One leaf may carry several concerns; these labels never create lanes\n46\tor replace required evals. Original intake text is retained in the review and\n47\tapplicable leaf constraints. Import rollback is tested before materialization.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7597863c-3440-4c56-85ee-92305db837e4","uuid":"1e614871-a773-4e68-973e-1bf19e37b3cf","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:11:03.817Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat i_tj56l9/.agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/decomposition.md","content":"# Native decomposition and review\n\nUse `taskspec decompose prepare <id> --recipe <file>` to validate authored input\nand propose topology. `--dry-run` produces diagnostics without changing the plan.\nEach accepted seam owns one swimlane; each capability leg names an observable\nstate and proof; executable leaves own coherent done-conditions and bounded writes.\nSDLC stages are concerns on the work, not mandatory lanes.\n\nA blocked proposal is a valid planning outcome. Preserve `OPEN` objections and\n`system_map.unknowns` when ownership, evidence, or product decisions are missing.\nKeep the authored proposal and report the smallest unresolved decision; do not\nclear unknowns or mark objections `ACCEPTED` or `FIXED` merely to make preparation\npass. Record resolution or accepted risk only from an explicit applicable decision.\nThe reviewer's identity authenticates review; it does not assign seam or swimlane\nownership. Record actual owners in the recipe and prepare the corrected topology\nbefore requesting review.\n\nRead `tasks/.plans/<id>/delivery-plan.yaml`, proposed leg artifacts, and graph\nbefore recording explicit human review:\n\n```bash\ntaskspec decompose review <id> --accept --reviewer <identity> --reason <decision>\ntaskspec decompose compile <id>\ntaskspec plan --manifest tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\ntaskspec batch --plan tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n```\n\nReview binds the complete topology through the repository HMAC key using the\nplan-review domain. Compilation and materialization do not seal execution.\nThe authored recipe, immutable snapshots, native TaskPlanLineage/v1, bundle,\nand existing materialization receipt retain the intent-to-leaf chain.\n\nBefore replanning, preserve the prior bundle path. Use `prepare --replace`, review,\ncompile, then `decompose impact <id> --against <prior-bundle.json>` to inspect\nchanged, added, removed, and unchanged projections. Relevant constraints, recipe,\ndependencies, proof, and source changes require renewed authorization. Unrelated\nsibling changes preserve the earlier snapshot for unchanged leaves.\n\nRecipe task fields may include `execution_recipe` (a strategy name),\n`shared_resources` (resource identifiers requiring serialization), and\n`proves_capabilities` (leg IDs this integration-proof leaf independently evaluates).\nAbsence of a proof leaf leaves a capability unproven even when all children are done.\n\nOptional `sdlc_stages` values are `plan`, `design`, `build`, `test`, `deploy`, and\n`maintain`. One leaf may carry several concerns; these labels never create lanes\nor replace required evals. Original intake text is retained in the review and\napplicable leaf constraints. Import rollback is tested before materialization.\n","numLines":48,"startLine":1,"totalLines":48}}}
